I’ve fixed the formal input representation to a symbolic flattened permutation `P` plus size `N`, with a definitional row-major grid constructor. This covers every valid `N×N` grid while letting the proof use guarded selectors for symbolic indexing. The selector lemmas only simplify data access; none bypasses Python control flow or supplies the final answer.
