The bounded residual found the cause: the generalized frame map accidentally allowed a synthetic `"$cells"` binding, so the prover explored closure-cell lookup states that the actual top-level `minPath` frame can never have. I’m narrowing each loop invariant to the exact plain-frame domain with `"$cells"` absent; this strengthens binding fidelity and removes a spurious execution branch.
