The exact-frame repair exposed a small base-case issue in my summary equations: at `J = N`, the summary relied on the prover deriving `N > oneCol`, even though the loop has plainly finished. I’m making the definition explicit—updates are possible only when `J < N`; otherwise the accumulator is preserved. This is a guard correction, not an execution bridge.
