Those bound facts were being simplified to `true`, which proved individual guard checks but erased the inequalities before the arithmetic implication needed them. I’m removing the erasing rewrites and retaining the bounds as explicit invariant facts, including at the entry. They are definitionally entailed by a permutation of `1..N²`; recording them explicitly keeps the solver’s linear arithmetic context intact.
