The bounded trace reaches the append, then the fixed `valSeqConcat` tries to recurse over the symbolic accumulated prefix—exactly the symbolic-collection access problem. I’m replacing that stuck functional term with a total `snocVS` data selector and expressing the loop summary as `appendPath(prefix, absolute_index, k, neighbor)`. Its recursion is simplification-only on an entailed one-step guard, so it cannot unroll past the circularity; the absolute index also pins the first element correctly for both total-length parities.
