The scan circularity now applies correctly. Its residual reveals a representation-level ambiguity: `gridRows` is an opaque total function, so unification does not infer that equal row structures came from the same flattened `P`. I’m pinning `P` in an otherwise-unused module-scope ghost binding `str(P)`. The program never looks up that name, and every claim preserves it; its constructor injectivity gives the circularity the missing identity without asserting a value equation.
